{
  "title": "20: Taa-Haa طه",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nطٰهٰ‌ ۚ‏(1)\nTAAHAA.\nTa Ha. (T. H.)\nمَاۤ اَنْزَلْنَا عَلَيْكَ الْقُرْاٰنَ لِتَشْقٰٓى ۙ‏(2)\nMAA ANZALNAA A’LAYKA QURAANA LETASHQAAA.\nO’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) Sent We not down the Qur’an unto thee that thou distressest thyself!\nاِلَّا تَذْكِرَةً لِّمَنْ يَّخْشٰى ۙ‏(3)\nILLAA TAZKERATANW LEMAN YAKHSHAA.\nSave it is a Reminder unto him who feareth (God)\nتَنْزِيْلًا مِّمَّنْ خَلَقَ الْاَرْضَ وَالسَّمٰوٰتِ الْعُلَى ؕ‏(4)\nTANZEELAA MIMMAYN KHALAQAL ARZA WA SAMAAWAATE AL-U’ULAA.\nIt is a Missive (sent down) from Him who created the earth and the heavens on high.\nاَلرَّحْمٰنُ عَلَى الْعَرْشِ اسْتَوٰى‏(5)\nAR-RAHMAAN A’LAL A’RSHIL TAWAA.\nThe Beneficent (God) on the ‘Arsh’ is firm\nلَهٗ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا وَمَا تَحْتَ الثَّرٰى‏(6)\nLAHU MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA WA MAA TAHTA AS-SARAA.\nHis is what is in the heavens and what is in the earth and what is between them two and what is beneath the lowest of the low below the earth.\nوَاِنْ تَجْهَرْ بِالْقَوْلِ فَاِنَّهٗ يَعْلَمُ السِّرَّ وَاَخْفٰى‏(7)\nWA TAJHAR BIL-QAWLE FA-INNAHU YA’LAMO AS-SERRA WAAKHFAA.\nAnd if thou utter aloud (or in whisper) Verily (alike) knoweth He (all that is) secret and (whatsoever is) yet more hidden.\nاَللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ ‌ؕ لَهُ الْاَسْمَآءُ الْحُسْنٰى‏(8)\nALLAAHO LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA LAHUL ASMAA-UL AL-HUSNAA.\nGod, there is no god but He; His are (all) the Best names.\n‌وَهَلْ اَتٰٮكَ حَدِيْثُ مُوْسٰى‌ۘ‏(9)\nWA HAL ATAAKA HADEESUL MOOSAA.\nAnd hath come unto thee the story of Moses?\nاِذْ رَاٰ نَارًا فَقَالَ لِاَهْلِهِ امْكُثُوْۤا اِنِّىْۤ اٰنَسْتُ نَارًا لَّعَلِّىْۤ اٰتِيْكُمْ مِّنْهَا بِقَبَسٍ اَوْ اَجِدُ عَلَى النَّارِ هُدًى‏(10)\nIZ RAA NAARAN FAQAALA LE-AHLEHIM KOSOO INNEE AANASTO NAARAN LA-A’LLEE AATEEKUM MINHAA BE-QABASIL AW AAJEDU A’LAL NAAR HODAM.\nWhen he saw fire, then said he unto his family, “Tarry ye here, for verily I perceive a fire: happly I may bring unto you a brand from it, or I find at the fire some guidance.\nفَلَمَّاۤ اَتٰٮهَا نُوْدِىَ يٰمُوْسٰىؕ‏(11)\nFALAMMAA ATAAHAA NOODEYA YAAMOOSAA.\nSo when he came unto it (the fire) a voice called: “O’ Moses!\nاِنِّىْۤ اَنَا رَبُّكَ فَاخْلَعْ نَعْلَيْكَ‌ۚ اِنَّكَ بِالْوَادِ الْمُقَدَّسِ طُوًىؕ‏(12)\nINNEE ANAA RABBOKA FAAKHLAA’ NAA’LAYKA INNAKA BIL-WAADE AL-MUQADDASE TOOAA.\nVerily I; I (alone) am thy Lord! So take off thy shoes! Verily thou art in the sacred valley of ‘Tuwa\nوَاَنَا اخْتَرْتُكَ فَاسْتَمِعْ لِمَا يُوْحٰى‏(13)\nANAT AKHTARTUKA FAASTAMEA’ LEMAKH YOOHAA.\nAnd I have chosen thee (for apostleship) then hearken thou unto what is revealed (unto thee)?\nاِنَّنِىْۤ اَنَا اللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنَا فَاعْبُدْنِىْ ۙ وَاَقِمِ الصَّلٰوةَ لِذِكْرِىْ‏(14)\nINNANEE ANAA LAAHO LAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANAA FAAA’BUDNEAA WA SALAATA LEZEKREAA.\nVerily I, I (alone) am God: There is no god but I: worship thou (only) Me, and establish prayer for My remembrance!\nاِنَّ السَّاعَةَ اٰتِيَةٌ اَكَادُ اُخْفِيْهَا لِتُجْزٰى كُلُّ نَفْسٍۢ بِمَا تَسْعٰى‏(15)\nINNAL SAA-A’TA AAATEETUN AAKAADU AUKHFEEHAA LETUJZAA KULLO NAFSIM BEMAA TASA’AA.\nVerily the Hour (of Doom) is sure to come but I am about to keep it hidden, so that every soul may be recompensed as he striveth:\nفَلَا يَصُدَّنَّكَ عَنْهَا مَنْ لَّا يُؤْمِنُ بِهَا وَاتَّبَعَ هَوٰٮهُ فَتَرْدٰى‏(16)\nFALAA YASUDDANNAKA A’NHAA MAN LAA BIL LAAHE BEHAA WA TABA-A’L HAWHU FATARDAA.\nTherefore let him who believeth not in it and followeth his own vain desires turn thee away from the truth, lest thou perish.\nوَمَا تِلْكَ بِيَمِيْنِكَ يٰمُوْسٰى‏(17)\nWA MAA TILKA BE-YAMEENEKA YAA MOOSAA.\nAnd what is this in thy hand O’ Moses!\nقَالَ هِىَ عَصَاىَ‌ۚ اَتَوَكَّؤُا عَلَيْهَا وَاَهُشُّ بِهَا عَلٰى غَنَمِىْ وَلِىَ فِيْهَا مَاٰرِبُ اُخْرٰى‏(18)\nQAALA HEYA A’ASAAAAA AATAWAKKAUA A’LAYHAA WAAHUSSHU BEHAA A’LAA GHANAMEAA WA LEYA FEEHAA MAAREBU LAHU.\nSaid he: “This is my staff; I recline on it, and I beat down leaves with it for my sheep, and for me therein are other uses (also).\nقَالَ اَلْقِهَا يٰمُوْسٰى‏(19)\nQAALA AALQEHAA YAA MOOSAA.\nHe said: “Cast it down, O’ Moses!\nفَاَلْقٰٮهَا فَاِذَا هِىَ حَيَّةٌ تَسْعٰى‏(20)\nFAALQAAHAA FA-EZAA HEYA HAYTUN TASA’AA.\nThen he cast it down, and lo! it was a serpent running.\nقَالَ خُذْهَا وَلَا تَخَفْ‌ سَنُعِيْدُهَا سِيْرَتَهَا الْاُوْلٰى‏(21)\nQAALA KHUZHAA WA LAA TAKHAF SANUE’EEDUHAA SEERATAHAA OOLAA.\nHe said: “Lay hold on it, and fear thou not; for We will restore it to its former state (of a staff)\nوَاضْمُمْ يَدَكَ اِلٰى جَنَاحِكَ تَخْرُجْ بَيْضَآءَ مِنْ غَيْرِ سُوْٓءٍ اٰيَةً اُخْرٰىۙ‏(22)\nWAAZMUM YADAKA ELAA JANAAHEKA TAKHRUJ BAYZAAA-A MIN GHAIRE SOOO-IN AAYATAL LAHU.\nAnd place thy hand under thy armpit, it shall come forth white, without any harm, (and this is) another sign (miracle),\nلِنُرِيَكَ مِنْ اٰيٰتِنَا الْكُبْرٰى‌ۚ‏(23)\nLENUREEKA MIN AAYAATENAA KUBRAA.\nThat We may show thee of Our greatersigns (miracles)\nاِذْهَبْ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ اِنَّهٗ طَغٰى‏(24)\nIZHAB ELAA FIR-A’WNA INNAHU TAGHAA.\nGo thou unto Pharaoh! Verily he hath transgressed the bounds!\nقَالَ رَبِّ اشْرَحْ لِىْ صَدْرِىْ ۙ‏(25)\nQAALA RABBISH RAHLEE SADREE. WA YASSIR LEE AMREE.\nSaid he “O’ My Lord! Expand for me my breast,\nوَيَسِّرْ لِىْۤ اَمْرِىْ ۙ‏(26)\nWAHLUL U’QDATAM MIN LESAANEE.\nAnd make easy for me my task,\nوَاحْلُلْ عُقْدَةً مِّنْ لِّسَانِیْ ۙ‏(27)\nYAFQAHOO QAWLEE.\nAnd loosen the knot of my tongue,\nيَفْقَهُوْا قَوْلِیْ ‏(28)\nYAFQAHOO QAWLEE.\n(That) they may understand my speech,\nوَاجْعَلْ لِّىْ وَزِيْرًا مِّنْ اَهْلِىْ ۙ‏(29)\nWA A’L LEE WAZEERAN MIN AAHLEAA.\nAnd appoint for me an aider from my family,\nهٰرُوْنَ اَخِى ۙ‏(30)\nAALO AAKHEAA.\nAaron my brother,\nاشْدُدْ بِهٖۤ اَزْرِىْ ۙ‏(31)\nASHDUD BEHI AAZREAA.\nStrengthen my back by him,\nوَاَشْرِكْهُ فِىْۤ اَمْرِىْ ۙ‏(32)\nWAASHREKHU FEE AMREE.\nAnd associate him (with me) in my affair,\nكَىْ نُسَبِّحَكَ كَثِيْرًا ۙ‏(33)\nKAY NUSABBEHAKA KASEERAA.\nThat we may glorify Thee much,\nوَّنَذْكُرَكَ كَثِيْرًا ؕ‏(34)\nWWANAZKURAKA KASEERAA.\nAnd remember Thee much\nاِنَّكَ كُنْتَ بِنَا بَصِيْرًا‏(35)\nINNAKA KUNTA LAKHASAFA BASEERAA.\nVerily Thou art ever seeing of us.\nقَالَ قَدْ اُوْتِيْتَ سُؤْلَكَ يٰمُوْسٰى‏(36)\nQAALA QAD AOOTEETA SULAKA YAA MOOSAA.\nSaid He: “Granted is thy prayer, O’ Moses!\nوَلَقَدْ مَنَنَّا عَلَيْكَ مَرَّةً اُخْرٰٓىۙ‏(37)\nWA LAQAD MANANNAA A’LAYKA MARRATAN AUKHRAAA.\nAnd indeed We conferred Our favour on thee at another time,\nاِذْ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلٰٓى اُمِّكَ مَا يُوْحٰٓى ۙ‏(38)\nIZ AAWHAYNAA ELAA AUMMEKA MAA YOOHAA.\nWhen We revealed unto thy mother what was revealed (unto her),\nاَنِ اقْذِفِيْهِ فِى التَّابُوْتِ فَاقْذِفِيْهِ فِى الْيَمِّ فَلْيُلْقِهِ الْيَمُّ بِالسَّاحِلِ يَاْخُذْهُ عَدُوٌّ لِّىْ وَعَدُوٌّ لَّهٗ‌ ؕ وَاَلْقَيْتُ عَلَيْكَ مَحَبَّةً مِّنِّىْ ۚ وَلِتُصْنَعَ عَلٰى عَيْنِىْ ۘ‏(39)\nSAALEHAN AQZEFEEHE FIL AT-TAABOOTE FAAQZEFEEHE FIL WA FALYULQEHE AL-YAMMU BEALSSAAHELE YAAKHUZHU A’DUWWUM LEE WA A’DUWWUM LAHU WAALQAYTU A’LAYKA MAHABBATAN MINNEE WALETUSNAA’A A’LAA A’AYNEAA.\nThat: “Cast him into a chest, then cast it into the sea, then the sea shall throw him ashore”; there taketh him (up) one (who is an) enemy unto Me and an enemy unto him; and I cast down upon thee love from Me (that everyone may love thee); so that thou mightest be brought up under My eyes (as I will):\nاِذْ تَمْشِىْۤ اُخْتُكَ فَتَقُوْلُ هَلْ اَدُلُّكُمْ عَلٰى مَنْ يَّكْفُلُهٗ‌ ؕ فَرَجَعْنٰكَ اِلٰٓى اُمِّكَ كَىْ تَقَرَّ عَيْنُهَا وَلَا تَحْزَنَ ؕ وَقَتَلْتَ نَفْسًا فَنَجَّيْنٰكَ مِنَ الْغَمِّ وَفَتَنّٰكَ فُتُوْنًا فَلَبِثْتَ سِنِيْنَ فِىْۤ اَهْلِ مَدْيَنَ ۙ ثُمَّ جِئْتَ عَلٰى قَدَرٍ يّٰمُوْسٰى‏(40)\nIZ TAMSHEE AUKHTUKA FA TAQOOLO HAL ADULLOKUM A’LAA MAN YYAKFULUH FARAJAA’NAAKA ELAA AUMMEKA KAY TAQARRA A’YNOHAA WA LAA TAHZANA WA NAFSAM NAFSAN FANAJJAYNAAKA MENAL AL-GHAMME WAFATANNAAKA FUTOONAN FALABESTA SENEEN FEE AHLIL MADYANA SUMMA BIL-HAQ A’LAA QADARIN YYAAMOOSAA.\nWhen thy sister went (unto Pharaoh’s wife) and said: “Shall I show you one who will take care of him?” So We brought thee back unto thy mother, that her eyes be cooled and she might grieve not; And thou didst kill a man (and wert perturbed) and We delivered thee from the grief and We tried thee with a heavy trial and then thou didst tarry years among the people of Midian, then thou didst come hither as ordained (by Us), O’ Moses!\nوَاصْطَنَعْتُكَ لِنَفْسِى‌ۚ‏(41)\nWAASTANAA’TUKA LENAFSEAA.\nAnd I have chosen thee for Myself;\nاِذْهَبْ اَنْتَ وَاَخُوْكَ بِاٰيٰتِىْ وَلَا تَنِيَا فِىْ ذِكْرِى‌ۚ‏(42)\nIZHAB ANTA WAAKHOOKA BE-AAYAATEE WA LAA TANEEA FEE ZEKREAA.\nGo thou and thy Brother with My signs (miracles) and slacken not either of you in remembering Me.\nاِذْهَبَاۤ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ اِنَّهٗ طَغٰى‌ ‌ۖۚ‌‌‌‏(43)\nAEZHABAA ELAA FIR-A’WNA INNAHU TAGHAA.\nGo ye both unto Pharaoh, Verily he hath transgressed (the bounds)\nفَقُوْلَا لَهٗ قَوْلًا لَّيِّنًا لَّعَلَّهٗ يَتَذَكَّرُ اَوْ يَخْشٰى‏(44)\nFAQOOLAA LAHU QAWLAM LLAYNAN LLAA’ALLAH YATAZAKKARU AW YAKHSHAA.\nThen speak ye both unto him a gentle word, happly he may get admonished or fear (Our punishment),\nقَالَا رَبَّنَاۤ اِنَّنَا نَخَافُ اَنْ يَّفْرُطَ عَلَيْنَاۤ اَوْ اَنْ يَّطْغٰى‏(45)\nQAALAA RABBANAA INNANAA NAKHAAFO AN YYAFRUTA A’LAYNAA AW AN YYATGHAA.\nSaid both “O’ Our Lord! Verily fear we that he breaketh forth against us, or lest he getteth uncontrolled.\nقَالَ لَا تَخَافَآ‌ اِنَّنِىْ مَعَكُمَاۤ اَسْمَعُ وَاَرٰى‏(46)\nQAALA LAA TAKHAAFAA INNANEE MAA’AKUMAA AASMAU’U WAARAA.\nSaid (God): “Fear not ye both! Verily I am with ye both; I do hear and see\nفَاْتِيٰهُ فَقُوْلَاۤ اِنَّا رَسُوْلَا رَبِّكَ فَاَرْسِلْ مَعَنَا بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ ۙ وَلَا تُعَذِّبْهُمْ‌ ؕ قَدْ جِئْنٰكَ بِاٰيَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ‌ ؕ وَالسَّلٰمُ عَلٰى مَنِ اتَّبَعَ الْهُدٰى‏(47)\nFAATEEHU FAQOOLAA INNAA RASOOLAA RABBEKA FAARSEL MAA’ANAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ WA LAA TUA’AZZEBHUM QAD JENAAKA BE-AAYATIL MIN RABBEKA WA SALAAMUL A’LAA MANIS TABA-A’L HODAA.\nSo go ye both unto him, and say”: “Verily we are apostles from thy Lord, so send thou with us the children of Israel, and torment them not! indeed have we brought signs (miracles) from thy Lord; and peace will be unto him who followeth the guidance;\nاِنَّا قَدْ اُوْحِىَ اِلَيْنَاۤ اَنَّ الْعَذَابَ عَلٰى مَنْ كَذَّبَ وَتَوَلّٰى‏(48)\nINNAA QAD OOHEYA ELAYNAA ANNAL A’ZAABA A’LAA MAN KAZZABA WA TAWALLAA.\nVerily, hath it been revealed unto us that indeed the chastisement shall certainly come upon him who belieth and turneth back.\nقَالَ فَمَنْ رَّبُّكُمَا يٰمُوْسٰى‏(49)\nQAALA FAMAN RRABBUKUMAA YAA MOOSAA.\nSaid (Pharaoh): “And who is the Lord of ye two, O’ Moses!\nقَالَ رَبُّنَا الَّذِىْۤ اَعْطٰى كُلَّ شَىْءٍ خَلْقَهٗ ثُمَّ هَدٰى‏(50)\nQAALA RABBONAA LAZEE A-A’TAA KULLA SHAY-IN KHALQAH SUMMA HADAA.\nSaid he (Moses): “Our Lord is He Who gave unto everything its (suitable) form, and then (also) guided it (aright)\nقَالَ فَمَا بَالُ الْقُرُوْنِ الْاُوْلٰى‏(51)\nQAALA FAMAA BAALU QOROONE OOLAA.\n(Pharaoh) said: “What then is the state of the generations past?\nقَالَ عِلْمُهَا عِنْدَ رَبِّىْ فِىْ كِتٰبٍ‌‌ۚ لَا يَضِلُّ رَبِّىْ وَلَا يَنْسَى‏(52)\nQAALA I’LMOHAA I’NDAL RABBEE FEE KETAABIM LAA YAZELLU RABBEE WA LAA YANSAA.\nHe said: “The knowledge thereof is with my Lord in a Book (secured by Him), erreth not my Lord, nor doth He forget.\nالَّذِىْ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الْاَرْضَ مَهْدًا وَّسَلَكَ لَكُمْ فِيْهَا سُبُلًا وَّ اَنْزَلَ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً ؕ فَاَخْرَجْنَا بِهٖۤ اَزْوَاجًا مِّنْ نَّبَاتٍ شَتّٰى‏(53)\nLAZEE JA-A’LA LAKOMUL ARZA MAHDAN WWASALAKA LAKUM FEEHAA SUBULAN WA ANZALAL MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN FA AKH-RAJNAA BEHI AZWAAJANW MIN NNABAATIN SHATTAA.\nHe Who made the earth for you a bed and made for you therein paths, and sent down from the heavens water; then thereby have We brought forth pairs of plants, various (in kinds)\nكُلُوْا وَارْعَوْا اَنْعَامَكُمْ‌ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّاُولِى النُّهٰى‏(54)\nKOLOO WAARA’AWA AANA’AAMAKUM INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEAOOLEAA AN-NUHAA.\nEat ye and pasture your cattle; Verily in this there are signs for those endowed with understanding\nمِنْهَا خَلَقْنٰكُمْ وَفِيْهَا نُعِيْدُكُمْ وَمِنْهَا نُخْرِجُكُمْ تَارَةً اُخْرٰى‏(55)\nMINHAA KHALAQNAAKUM WA FEEHAA NUE’EEDUKUM WA MINHAA NUKHREJUKUM TAARATAN LAHU.\nFrom it (the earth) We created you, and into it will We return you, and out of it will We bring you forth for a second time.\nوَلَقَدْ اَرَيْنٰهُ اٰيٰتِنَا كُلَّهَا فَكَذَّبَ وَاَبٰى‏(56)\nWA LAQAD AARAYNAAHU AAYAATENAA KULLAHAA FA KAZZABA WA ABAA.\nAnd indeed We did show unto him Our signs, all of them, but he belied and refused (to believe)\nقَالَ اَجِئْتَنَا لِتُخْرِجَنَا مِنْ اَرْضِنَا بِسِحْرِكَ يٰمُوْسٰى‏(57)\nQAALA AAJETANAA LETUKHREJANAA MIN ARZENAA BESEHREKA YAA MOOSAA.\nSaid he: “Hast thou come unto us that thou turneth us out of our land by thy sorcery, O’ Moses!\nفَلَنَاْتِيَنَّكَ بِسِحْرٍ مِّثْلِهٖ فَاجْعَلْ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكَ مَوْعِدًا لَّا نُخْلِفُهٗ نَحْنُ وَلَاۤ اَنْتَ مَكَانًا سُوًى‏(58)\nFALANAATEENNAKA BESEHRIN MISLEH FAJ-A’L BAYNANAA WA WA MAWE’EDAN LAA NUKHLEFUH NAHNO WA LAA ANTA MAKAANAN SOOAA.\nThen we too will certainly produce before thee a sorcery like unto it, so make between us and thee a tryst, we will not fail it, (neither) we nor thou, in a place alike for both\nقَالَ مَوْعِدُكُمْ يَوْمُ الزِّيْنَةِ وَاَنْ يُّحْشَرَ النَّاسُ ضُحًى‏(59)\nQAALA MAWE’EDUKUM YAWMUD AZ-ZEENATE WA YYUHSHARA NAASO ZUHAN.\n(Moses) said: “Your tryst be the day of the Festival, and let the people be gathered together in the bright of the noon.\nفَتَوَلّٰى فِرْعَوْنُ فَجَمَعَ كَيْدَهٗ ثُمَّ اَتٰى‏(60)\nFA TAWALLAA FIRA’WNO FA JAMA-A’ KAYDAH SUMMA ATAA.\nSo Pharaoh turned back and collected his crafts thereafter he came.\nقَالَ لَهُمْ مُّوْسٰى وَيْلَكُمْ لَا تَفْتَرُوْا عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا فَيُسْحِتَكُمْ بِعَذَابٍ‌ۚ وَقَدْ خَابَ مَنِ افْتَرٰى‏(61)\nQAALA LAHUM MOOSAA WAYLAKUM LAA TAFTAROOA A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAN FAYUSHETAKUM BE-A’ZAABIN WA QAD QAD MANIS TARAA.\nSaid Moses unto them, “Woe unto you! forge ye not a lie against God: lest He destroyeth you by a sorcery. And faileth he who forgeth a lie.\nفَتَنَازَعُوْۤا اَمْرَهُمْ بَيْنَهُمْ وَاَسَرُّوا النَّجْوٰى‏(62)\nFATANAAZAU’OOA AAMRAHUM BAYNAHUM WAASARROOA AN-NAJWAA.\nThen they (the magicians) disputed about their affair among themselves and they spake apart in secret.\nقَالُوْۤا اِنْ هٰذٰٮنِ لَسٰحِرٰنِ يُرِيْدٰنِ اَنْ يُّخْرِجٰكُمْ مِّنْ اَرْضِكُمْ بِسِحْرِهِمَا وَيَذْهَبَا بِطَرِيْقَتِكُمُ الْمُثْلٰى‏(63)\nQAALOO IN HAAZAANE LASAAHERAANE YUREEDAANE AN YYUKHREJAAKUM MIN AARZEKUM BESEHREHEMAA WAYAZHABAA BETAREEQATEKUMU AL-MUSLAA.\n(At last) Said they: “These two are certainly two (expert) sorcerers who intend to drive you out from your land by the sorcery of them both and wipe out your most exemplary tradition!\nفَاَجْمِعُوْا كَيْدَكُمْ ثُمَّ ائْتُوْا صَفًّا‌ ۚ وَقَدْ اَفْلَحَ الْيَوْمَ مَنِ اسْتَعْلٰى‏(64)\nFAAJMEU’OOA KAYDAKUM SUMMA ATOOA MALAAA-EKATO WA QAD AFLAHA YAWMA MANIS ASTAA’LAA.\nSo muster your plan: then come in (organized) order: And indeed shall succeed he this day who overcometh!\nقَالُوْا يٰمُوْسٰٓى اِمَّاۤ اَنْ تُلْقِىَ وَاِمَّاۤ اَنْ نَّكُوْنَ اَوَّلَ مَنْ اَلْقٰى‏(65)\nQAALOO MOOSAA IMMAA AN TULQEAAA WA AMMAA AN NNAKOONA AWWALA MAN AALQAA.\nThey said: “O’ Moses! Either cast thou (first) or shall we be the first who cast down?\nقَالَ بَلْ اَلْقُوْا‌ۚ فَاِذَا حِبَالُهُمْ وَعِصِيُّهُمْ يُخَيَّلُ اِلَيْهِ مِنْ سِحْرِهِمْ اَنَّهَا تَسْعٰى‏(66)\nQAALA BAL AALQOOA FA-EZAA HEBAALUHUM WAE’ESEEHUM YUKHAYLU ELAYHE MIN SEHREHEM AANNAHAA TASA’AA.\n(Moses) said: “Nay! cast ye down (first) Then lo! Their cords and their rods, seemed to him by their sorcery as if they were running.\nفَاَوْجَسَ فِىْ نَفْسِهٖ خِيْفَةً مُّوْسٰى‏(67)\nFAAWJASA FEE WA KHEEFATAN MOOSAA.\nThen Moses felt in himself a fear.\nقُلْنَا لَا تَخَفْ اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ الْاَعْلٰى‏(68)\nQULNAL LAA TAKHAF INNAKA ANTA A-A’LAA.\nSaid We: “Fear thou not! Verily thou shalt be the uppermost.\nوَاَ لْقِ مَا فِىْ يَمِيْنِكَ تَلْقَفْ مَا صَنَعُوْا‌ ؕاِنَّمَا صَنَعُوْا كَيْدُ سٰحِرٍ‌ ؕ وَلَا يُفْلِحُ السّٰحِرُ حَيْثُ اَتٰى‏(69)\nWA ALQE MAA FEE YAMEENEKA TALQAF MAA SANAO’O, INNAMAA SANAO’O KAYDO SAAHERIN, WA LAA YUFLEHUS SAAHERO HAYSO ATAA.\nAnd cast down what is in thy right hand: It shall swallow up what they have wrought; Verily they have wrought by the plan of a sorcerer, and a sorcerer shall not be successful whatso ever manner (of skill) he may come from.\nفَاُلْقِىَ السَّحَرَةُ سُجَّدًا قَالُوْۤا اٰمَنَّا بِرَبِّ هٰرُوْنَ وَمُوْسٰى‏(70)\nFA ULQEYA AS-SAHARATU SUJJADANW QAALOO AAMANNAA BE RABBIL AALO WA MOOSAA.\nThen fell down the sorcerers prostrating (in obeisance) they said: “We believe in the Lord of Aaron and Moses!\nقَالَ اٰمَنْتُمْ لَهٗ قَبْلَ اَنْ اٰذَنَ لَكُمْ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ لَكَبِيْرُكُمُ الَّذِىْ عَلَّمَكُمُ السِّحْرَ‌ۚ فَلَاُقَطِّعَنَّ اَيْدِيَكُمْ وَاَرْجُلَكُمْ مِّنْ خِلَافٍ وَّلَاُصَلِّبَنَّكُمْ فِىْ جُذُوْعِ النَّخْلِ وَلَتَعْلَمُنَّ اَيُّنَاۤ اَشَدُّ عَذَابًا وَّاَبْقٰى‏(71)\nQAALA AAMANTUM LAHU QABLA AN AAAZANA LAKUM INNAHU LAKABEERUKUMU LAZEE A’ALLAMAKUMU SEHR FALAAQATTEA’ANNA AAYDEEKUM WAARJULAKUM MIN KHELAAFIN WWALAASALLEBANNAKUM FEE JUZOOE’E AN-NAKHLE WALATAA’LAMUNNA AAYNAA ASHADDO A’ZAABAN KHAYRUWN.\nSaid (Pharaoh): “Believe ye in him ere I give ye leave (to do it)? Verily he is your Chief (sorcerer) who hath taught you sorcery, so I shall certainly cut off your hands and your feet on the opposite sides, and I will certainly crucify you on the trunks of the palm trees, then will ye certainly know which of us is more severe in tormenting and abiding!\nقَالُوْا لَنْ نُّؤْثِرَكَ عَلٰى مَا جَآءَنَا مِنَ الْبَيِّنٰتِ وَالَّذِىْ فَطَرَنَا‌ فَاقْضِ مَاۤ اَنْتَ قَاضٍ‌ ؕ اِنَّمَا تَقْضِىْ هٰذِهِ الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَا ؕ‏(72)\nQAALOO LAN NNUSERAKA A’LAA MAA JAAA-ANAA MENAL BAYYENAATE WAL LAZEE FATARANAA FAAQZE MAA ANTA QAAZIN INNAMAA TAQZEAA HAAZEHE HAYAATAD DUNYAA.\nThey said: “Never will we prefer thee (O’ Pharaoh!) to what hath come unto us of the clear signs, and to Him Who made us, so decree thou whatever decree thou decreeth; for thou canst decree only about the life of this world\nاِنَّاۤ اٰمَنَّا بِرَبِّنَا لِيَغْفِرَ لَنَا خَطٰيٰنَا وَمَاۤ اَكْرَهْتَنَا عَلَيْهِ مِنَ السِّحْرِؕ‌ وَاللّٰهُ خَيْرٌ وَّاَبْقٰى‏(73)\nINNAA AAMANNAA BERABBENAA LEEGHFERA LANAA KHATAAYAANAA WA MAA AAKRAHTANAA A’LAYHE MENAL AS-SEHRE WAL LAAHO KHAYRUL KHAYRUWN.\nVerily we! we do believe in our Lord that He may forgive us our sins and the sorcery thou didst compel us (to do); and God is the Best and the Most Abiding!\nاِنَّهٗ مَنْ يَّاْتِ رَبَّهٗ مُجْرِمًا فَاِنَّ لَهٗ جَهَنَّمَ‌ۚ لَا يَمُوْتُ فِيْهَا وَ لَا يَحْيٰى‏(74)\nINNAHU MAN INY WAL MUJREMAN FA-INNAL LAHU JAHANNAMA LAA YAMOOTO FEEHAA WA LAA YAHYAA.\nAnd verily he who cometh unto his Lord as guilty, for him certainly is Hell; he shall die not in it nor shall he live.\nوَمَنْ يَّاْتِهٖ مُؤْمِنًا قَدْ عَمِلَ الصّٰلِحٰتِ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمُ الدَّرَجٰتُ الْعُلٰىۙ‏(75)\nWA MAN YYAATEH MUMENAN QAD A’MELA SAALEHAATE FA-OOLAAA-EKA LAHOMUL AD-DARAJAATU AL-U’ULAA.\nAnd whosoever cometh unto Him as a believer and who hath indeed done good deeds, these, for them are the ranks high,\nجَنّٰتُ عَدْنٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا‌ ؕ وَذٰ لِكَ جَزَآءُ مَنْ تَزَكّٰى‏(76)\nJANNAATU A’ADNIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA WAZAA LEKA JAZAAA-O MAN TAZAKKAA.\nThe Gardens of Eternity, beneath which flow rivers, to abide therein; and this is the recompense of him who purifieth himself (from evil).\nوَلَقَدْ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلٰى مُوْسٰٓى ۙ اَنْ اَسْرِ بِعِبَادِىْ فَاضْرِبْ لَهُمْ طَرِيْقًا فِى الْبَحْرِ يَبَسًا ۙ لَّا تَخٰفُ دَرَكًا وَّلَا تَخْشٰى‏(77)\nWA LAQAD AAWHAYNAA ELAA MOOSAA AN AASRE BE-E’BAADEE FAAZREB LAHUM TAREEQAN FIL BAHRE YABASAN LAA TAKHAAFU DARAKAN WA LAA TAKHSHAA.\nAnd indeed We revealed unto Moses (saying); “Travel thou by night with My servants, and strike for them a dry path in the sea, not fearing to be overtaken (by Pharaoh), nor be thou afraid (of getting drowned)\nفَاَتْبَعَهُمْ فِرْعَوْنُ بِجُنُوْدِهٖ فَغَشِيَهُمْ مِّنَ الْيَمِّ مَا غَشِيَهُمْؕ‏(78)\nFAATBAA’AHUM FIRA’WNO BEJUNOODEH FAGHASHEEHUM MENAL WA MAA GHASHEEHUM.\nAnd followed them Pharaoh with his hosts, so covered them (the billows) of the sea, as they were they covered (drowned).\nوَاَضَلَّ فِرْعَوْنُ قَوْمَهٗ وَمَا هَدٰى‏(79)\nWA AZALLAL FIRA’WNO QAWMAH WA MAA HADAA.\nAnd Pharaoh led astray his people and he did not guide them (aright)\nيٰبَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ قَدْ اَنْجَيْنٰكُمْ مِّنْ عَدُوِّكُمْ وَوٰعَدْنٰكُمْ جَانِبَ الطُّوْرِ الْاَيْمَنَ وَنَزَّلْنَا عَلَيْكُمُ الْمَنَّ وَالسَّلْوٰى‏(80)\nYAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ QAD AANJAYNAAKUM MIN A’ADOOKUM WAWA’ADNAAKUM JAANEBA TOORE AL-AAYMANA WA NAZZALNAA A’LAYKOMUL MANNA WAALSSALWAA.\n(“O’ Children of Israel!) We rescued you from your foe; and We made a covenant with of Israel!) you on the right side of ‘Tur’ (the Mount Sinai), and We sent down unto you Manna and quails:\nكُلُوْا مِنْ طَيِّبٰتِ مَا رَزَقْنٰكُمْ وَلَا تَطْغَوْا فِيْهِ فَيَحِلَّ عَلَيْكُمْ غَضَبِىْ‌ۚ وَمَنْ يَّحْلِلْ عَلَيْهِ غَضَبِىْ فَقَدْ هَوٰى‏(81)\nKOLOO MIN TAYYEBAATE MAA RAZAQNAAKUM WA LAA TATGHAW FEEHE FAYAHELLA A’LAYKUM GHAZABEAA WA MAN YYAHLEL A’LAYHE GHAZABEAA FAQAD HAWAA.\nEat ye of the good things We have provided you with and transgress not in it, lest descendeth on you My wrath, and on whomsoever My wrath doth descend, indeed he is perished.\nوَاِنِّىْ لَغَفَّارٌ لِّمَنْ تَابَ وَاٰمَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَالِحًا ثُمَّ اهْتَدٰى‏(82)\nWA INNEE LAGHAFFAARUN LEMAN TAABA WA AAMANA WA A’MELA SAALEHAN SUMMA TADAA.\nAnd verily I am the Most Forgiving unto him who repenteth and believeth and doth good, then he doth continue to follow the right guidance.\nوَمَاۤ اَعْجَلَكَ عَنْ قَوْمِكَ يٰمُوْسٰى‏(83)\nWA MAA AAA’JALAKA A’N QAWMEKA YAA MOOSAA.\n(Said God): “But what made thee hasten (thyself on apart) from thy people, O’ Moses!\nقَالَ هُمْ اُولَاۤءِ عَلٰٓى اَثَرِىْ وَ عَجِلْتُ اِلَيْكَ رَبِّ لِتَرْضٰى‏(84)\nQAALA HUM AOOLAAE A’LAA AASAREAA WA A’AJELTU ELAYKA RABBE LE-TARZAA.\nSaid (Moses): “They are close on my track and I hastened unto Thee O’ my Lord! that thou mightest be well pleased (with me)!\nقَالَ فَاِنَّا قَدْ فَتَنَّا قَوْمَكَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِكَ وَاَضَلَّهُمُ السَّامِرِىُّ‏(85)\nQAALA FAINNAA QAD FATANNAL QAWMAKA MIN BAA’DEKA WAAZALLAHUMU AS-SAAMEREAAAU.\nSaid (God): “Verily We have tried thy people in thine absence, and the Samiri had led them astray.\nفَرَجَعَ مُوْسَىٰۤ اِلٰى قَوْمِهٖ غَضْبَانَ اَسِفًا  ۙ قَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اَلَمْ يَعِدْكُمْ رَبُّكُمْ وَعْدًا حَسَنًا  ۙ اَفَطَالَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْعَهْدُ اَمْ اَرَدْتُّمْ اَنْ يَّحِلَّ عَلَيْكُمْ غَضَبٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ فَاَخْلَفْتُمْ مَّوْعِدِىْ‏(86)\nFARAJAA’A MOOSAA ELAA QAWMEHI GHAZBAANA AASEFAN QAALA LE-QAWMEHI ALAM YAE’EDKUM RABBOKUM WA’DAN HASANAN AAFATAALA A’LAYKOMUL AL-A’AHDU AM ARAD-TUM AN YYAHELLA A’LAYKUM GHAZABUN MIN RABBEKUM FAAKHLAFTUM MMAWE’EDEAA.\nSo returned Moses unto his people angered, sorrowfully said he! “O’ my people! Did not your Lord promise you a goodly promise? Did then the promise seem long to you? or did ye wish, or desired ye that the wrath from your Lord should light upon you? that ye violated the tryst with me?\nقَالُوْا مَاۤ اَخْلَفْنَا مَوْعِدَكَ بِمَلْكِنَا وَلٰكِنَّا حُمِّلْنَاۤ اَوْزَارًا مِّنْ زِيْنَةِ الْقَوْمِ فَقَذَفْنٰهَا فَكَذٰلِكَ اَلْقَى السَّامِرِىُّ ۙ‏(87)\nQAALOO MAA AAKHLAFNAA MAWE’EDAKA BEMALKENAA WA LAAKINNAA HUMMELNAA AAWZAARAN MIN ZEENATE QAWMIL FAQAZAFNAAHAA FA KAZAALEKA AALQAA AS-SAAMEREAAAU.\nSaid they: “We violated not the tryst with thee of our own accord, but we were made to bear the burdens of the ornaments of the people, so we cast them away, and thus didst the Samiri suggest\nفَاَخْرَجَ لَهُمْ عِجْلًا جَسَدًا لَّهٗ خُوَارٌ فَقَالُوْا هٰذَاۤ اِلٰهُكُمْ وَاِلٰهُ مُوْسٰى  فَنَسِىَ‏(88)\nFA-AKHRAJA LAHUM E’EJLAN JASADAN LAHU KHOOARUN FA-QAALOO HAAZAA ELAAHOKUM WAALAAHU MOOSAA FANASEAAA.\nThen he brought forth (from the fire) for them (the image of) a calf, a (mere) body; which (also) gave out the lowing sound; Then they said: “This is your god and the god of Moses, but he (Moses) hath forgotten,\nاَفَلَا يَرَوْنَ اَلَّا يَرْجِعُ اِلَيْهِمْ قَوْلًا ۙ وَّلَا يَمْلِكُ لَهُمْ ضَرًّا وَّلَا نَفْعًا‏(89)\nAFALAA YARAWNAL ALLAA YARJE-O’L ELAYHIM QAWLAM WA LAA YAMLEKU LAHUM BEKUM WA LAA BEKUM.\nWhat! See they not that it could not return unto them a word (for an answer) and that it could neither hurt nor benefit them?\nوَلَقَدْ قَالَ لَهُمْ هٰرُوْنُ مِنْ قَبْلُ يٰقَوْمِ اِنَّمَا فُتِنْتُمْ بِهٖ‌ۚ وَاِنَّ رَبَّكُمُ الرَّحْمٰنُ فَاتَّبِعُوْنِىْ وَاَطِيْعُوْۤا اَمْرِىْ‏(90)\nWA LAQAD QAALA LAHUM HAAROONO MIN QABLO LE-QAWMEHI INNAMAA FUTENTUM BEHI WA INNA RABBAKOMUL RAHMAANO FAATTABEU’OONEAA WAATEEU’OOA AMREE.\nAnd indeed Aaron had said unto them before: “O’ my people! Verily, ye are tried by it (the image) and verily your Lord is the Beneficent (God), so follow me and obey ye my order.\nقَالُوْا لَنْ نَّبْرَحَ عَلَيْهِ عٰكِفِيْنَ حَتّٰى يَرْجِعَ اِلَيْنَا مُوْسٰى‏(91)\nQAALOO LAN NNABRAHA A’LAYHE A’AAKEFEENA HATTAA YARJEA’A ELAYNAA MOOSAA.\nSaid they: “Never will we cease worshipping it until returneth unto us Moses.\nقَالَ يٰهٰرُوْنُ مَا مَنَعَكَ اِذْ رَاَيْتَهُمْ ضَلُّوْٓا ۙ‏(92)\nQAALA YAA HAAROONO MAA MANAA’AKA IZ RA-AYTAHUM ZALLOOA.\n(Moses) said: “O’ Aaron! What hindered thee when thou didst see them going astray,\nاَلَّا تَتَّبِعَنِ‌ؕ اَفَعَصَيْتَ اَمْرِىْ‏(93)\nALLAA TATTABEA’ANE AAFAA’ASAYTA AMREE.\nThat thou didst not follow me? Hast thou then disobeyed my order?\nقَالَ يَابْنَؤُمَّ لَا تَاْخُذْ بِلِحْيَتِىْ وَلَا بِرَاْسِىْ‌ۚ اِنِّىْ خَشِيْتُ اَنْ تَقُوْلَ فَرَّقْتَ بَيْنَ بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ وَلَمْ تَرْقُبْ قَوْلِىْ‏(94)\nQAALA YAABNAUMMA LAA TAAKHUZ BELEHYATEAA WA LAA BERAASEAA INNEE KHASHEETU AN TAQOOLA FARRAQTA BAYNA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ WA LAM TARQUB QAWLEAA.\nSaid (Aaron): “O’ son of my mother! Seize me not by my beard nor by my head; I was afraid lest sayest thou: “Thou hast caused a division among the children of Israel and didst not respect my word!\nقَالَ فَمَا خَطْبُكَ يٰسَامِرِىُّ‏(95)\nQAALA FAMAA KHATBUKA YAASAAMEREAAAU.\n(Moses) said: “What was thy object O’ Samiri?\nقَالَ بَصُرْتُ بِمَا لَمْ يَبْصُرُوْا بِهٖ فَقَبَضْتُ قَبْضَةً مِّنْ اَثَرِ الرَّسُوْلِ فَنَبَذْتُهَا وَكَذٰلِكَ سَوَّلَتْ لِىْ نَفْسِى‏(96)\nQAALA BASURTU BEMAA LAM YABSUROOA BEHI FAQABAZTU QABZATAN MIN WOJOOHEHIM RASOOLE FANABAZTUHAA WA KAZAALEKA SAWLAT LEE NAFSEAA.\nSaid (Samiri): “I saw what they did not see, so I took a handful of (the dust) from the track of the Messenger (Angel), and flung it (into the image of the calf) for so did my self prompt me (to do)\nقَالَ فَاذْهَبْ فَاِنَّ لَكَ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ اَنْ تَقُوْلَ لَا مِسَاسَ‌ وَاِنَّ لَكَ مَوْعِدًا لَّنْ تُخْلَفَهٗ‌ ۚ وَانْظُرْ اِلٰٓى اِلٰهِكَ الَّذِىْ ظَلْتَ عَلَيْهِ عَاكِفًا‌ ؕ لَّنُحَرِّقَنَّهٗ ثُمَّ لَنَنْسِفَنَّهٗ فِى الْيَمِّ نَسْفًا‏(97)\nQAALA FAAZHAB FA-INNAL LAKA FIL HAYAATID AN TAQOOLA LAA MESAASA WA INNA LAKA MAWE’EDAN LAN-Y TUKHLAFAH AAYATAL ELAA AELAAHEKA LAZEE ZALTA A’LAYHE A’AAKEFAN LLANUHARREQANNAH SUMMA LANANSEFANNAH FIL WA NASFAN.\n(Moses) said: “Begone then, verily for thee it shall be in this life to say: ‘Touch me not’; and (besides this) thou hast a tryst (of punishment) never will that fail; and (now) look at thy god whose worship thou kept (so long); Certainly will we burn it, then certainly will we scatter (the ashes of) it in the sea (with a wide) scattering!\nاِنَّمَاۤ اِلٰهُكُمُ اللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ‌ؕ وَسِعَ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ عِلْمًا‏(98)\nINNAMAA AELAAHUKUMU LAAHO LAZEE LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOO WASEA’ KULLA SHAY-IN I’LMAN.\nVerily your God is only ‘Allah’ (God); There is no god but He; He comprehendeth all things in (His) knowledge!\nكَذٰلِكَ نَقُصُّ عَلَيْكَ مِنْ اَنْۢبَآءِ مَا قَدْ سَبَقَ‌ ۚ وَقَدْ اٰتَيْنٰكَ مِنْ لَّدُنَّا ذِكْرًا ‌ ۖ‌ ۚ‏(99)\nKAZAALEKA NAQUSSU A’LAYKA MIN AANBAAE MAA QAD SABAQA WA QAD AAATAYNAAKA MIN WA ZIKRAA.\nThus do We relate unto thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) of the (historic) accounts of what hath passed (of old); and indeed have We given unto thee from Ourselves a Reminder (Qur’an).\nمَنْ اَعْرَضَ عَنْهُ فَاِنَّهٗ يَحْمِلُ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ وِزْرًا ۙ‏(100)\nMAN A-A’RAZA A’NHO FA-INNAHU YAHMELO YAWMA QEYAAMATE WEZRAN.\nWhosoever turneth aside from it, verily he shall bear on the Day of Resurrection, a burden,\nخٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهِ‌ ؕ وَسَآءَ لَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ حِمْلًا ۙ‏(101)\nKHAALEDEENA FEEHE WA SAAA-A LAHUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE HEMLAN.\nAbiding in it; while grievous will it be for them on the Day of Resurrection to bear,\nيَّوْمَ يُنْفَخُ فِى الصُّوْرِ‌ وَنَحْشُرُ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ يَوْمَئِذٍ زُرْقًا‌ ۖ ‌ۚ‏(102)\nYAWMA YUNFAKHO FIL SOORE WA NAHSHORO MUJREMEEN YAWMA-EZIN ZURQAN.\n(On) the day when the Trumpet shall be blown and We will gather the guilty ones, and the blue eyed ones.\nيَّتَخَافَتُوْنَ بَيْنَهُمْ اِنْ لَّبِثْتُمْ اِلَّا عَشْرًا‏(103)\nYYATAKHAAFATOONA BAYNAHUM IN LLABESTUM ILLAA A’SHRAN.\nThey shall consult among themselves in a low voice (saying): “Ye did tarry but ten (days)\nنَحْنُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا يَقُوْلُوْنَ اِذْ يَقُوْلُ اَمْثَلُهُمْ طَرِيْقَةً اِنْ لَّبِثْتُمْ اِلَّا يَوْمًا‏(104)\nNAHNO A-A’LAMO BEMAA YAQOOLOONA IZ YAQOOLO AAMSALUHUM TAREEQATAN IN LLABESTUM ILLAA YAWMAN.\nWe know best what they will say, when the most ideal ones of them in conduct will say: “Ye tarried not but a day!\nوَيَسْئَلُوْنَكَ عَنِ الْجِبَالِ فَقُلْ يَنْسِفُهَا رَبِّىْ نَسْفًا ۙ‏(105)\nYAS-ALOONAKA A’NIL JEBAALE FAQUL YANSEFUHAA RABBEE NASFAN.\nAnd they ask thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) about (what will happen to) the mountains (on the Day of Resurrection), say then, “My Lord will root them up and scatter them away as dust,\nفَيَذَرُهَا قَاعًا صَفْصَفًا ۙ‏(106)\nFAYAZARUHAA QAAA’AN SAFSAFAN.\nThen leave it a plain, smooth level,\nلَّا تَرٰى فِيْهَا عِوَجًا وَّلَاۤ اَمْتًا ؕ‏(107)\nLAA TARAA FEEHAA E’EWAJAN WA LAA AAMTAN.\nThou shall see not in it any crookedness or unevenness\nيَوْمَئِذٍ يَّتَّبِعُوْنَ الدَّاعِىَ لَا عِوَجَ لَهٗ‌ؕ وَخَشَعَتِ الْاَصْوَاتُ لِلرَّحْمٰنِ فَلَا تَسْمَعُ اِلَّا هَمْسًا‏(108)\nYAWMA-EZIN YYATTABEU’OONA AD-DAAE’EAAA LAA E’EWAJA LAHU WAKHASHAA’ATE AL-AASWAATU LELRRAHMAANE FALAA TASMAU’U ILLAA HAMSAN.\nOn that day they shall follow the summoner no crookedness (shall be shown) unto him, and low shall be the voices before the Beneficent (God), that thou shalt hear not aught but the light footfall.\nيَوْمَئِذٍ لَّا تَنْفَعُ الشَّفَاعَةُ اِلَّا مَنْ اَذِنَ لَهُ الرَّحْمٰنُ وَرَضِىَ لَهٗ قَوْلًا‏(109)\nYAWMA-EZIN LAA TANFAU’U ASH-SHAFAAA’ATU ILLAA MAN AZENA LAHUL RAHMAANO WA RAZEYAL LAHU QAWLAM.\nOn that day shall avail not intercession (of any) save (that of) whom hath permitted God, and whose word He is pleased with.\nيَعْلَمُ مَا بَيْنَ اَيْدِيْهِمْ وَمَا خَلْفَهُمْ وَلَا يُحِيْطُوْنَ بِهٖ عِلْمًا‏(110)\nYA’LAMO MAA BAYNA AYDEEHIM WA MAA KHALFAHUM WA LAA YOHEETOONA BEHI I’LMAN.\nKnoweth He what is before them and what is behind them, while they comprehend Him not in (their) knowledge.\nوَعَنَتِ الْوُجُوْهُ لِلْحَىِّ الْقَيُّوْمِ‌ؕ وَقَدْ خَابَ مَنْ حَمَلَ ظُلْمًا‏(111)\nWAA’ANATE AL-WUJOOHU LIL-HAA AL-QAYWME WA QAD QAD MAN HAMALA ZULMAWN.\nAnd (all) faces shall be humbled before the Ever-Living, The Self- Subsistent God, and indeed disappointed will be he who beareth iniquity.\nوَمَنْ يَّعْمَلْ مِنَ الصّٰلِحٰتِ وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ فَلَا يَخٰفُ ظُلْمًا وَّلَا هَضْمًا‏(112)\nWA MAN YA’MAL MENAL SAALEHAATE WA HOWA MUMENUN FALAA YAKHAAFU ZULMAWN WA LAA HAZMAN.\nAnd whosoever doth good deeds and he be a believer, he shall fear not of (the least) injustice (unto him), nor of (any) curtailment (of his dues).\nوَكَذٰلِكَ اَنْزَلْنٰهُ قُرْاٰنًا عَرَبِيًّا وَّ صَرَّفْنَا فِيْهِ مِنَ الْوَعِيْدِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَّقُوْنَ اَوْ يُحْدِثُ لَهُمْ ذِكْرًا‏(113)\nWA KAZAALEKA ANZALNAAHO QURAANAN A’RABIYYAL WA SARRAFNAA FEEHE MENAL AL-WAE’EEDE LA-A’LLAHUM YATTAQOON AW LAAHA LAHUM ZIKRAA.\nThus have We sent down (unto thee O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) an Arabic Qur’an and explained therein some of the threats, that they may adopt piety or that it may serve unto them a reminder.\nفَتَعٰلَى اللّٰهُ الْمَلِكُ الْحَقُّ‌ ۚ وَلَا تَعْجَلْ بِالْقُرْاٰنِ مِنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ يُّقْضٰٓى اِلَيْكَ وَحْيُهٗ‌ وَقُلْ رَّبِّ زِدْنِىْ عِلْمًا‏(114)\nFA TA-A’ALAL LAAHO AL-MALEKU HAQQO WA LAA TAA’JAL BE-QUR-AANE MIN QABLE AN YYUQZAAA ELAYKA WAHYUH WA QUL RABBIL ZEDNEAA I’LMAN.\nHigh above all is God, the King, the (Self-Existent) Truth; And hasten not (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) with the Qur’an ere its completed unto thee its revelation, and say thou: “O’ my Lord! increase me in knowledge!\nوَلَقَدْ عَهِدْنَاۤ اِلٰٓى اٰدَمَ مِنْ قَبْلُ فَنَسِىَ وَلَمْ نَجِدْ لَهٗ عَزْمًا‏(115)\nWA LAQAD A’AHEDNAA ELAA AADAMAL MIN QABLO FANASEAAA WA LAM NAJED LAHU A’AZMAN.\nAnd indeed had We covenanted unto Adam before, but he forgot; but We did not find in him any intention (to disobey Us).\nوَاِذْ قُلْنَا لِلْمَلٰٓئِكَةِ اسْجُدُوْا لِاٰدَمَ فَسَجَدُوْۤا اِلَّاۤ اِبْلِيْسَؕ اَبٰى‏(116)\nWA IZ QULNAL LIL-MALAAA-EKATE JODOO LE-AADAMA FASAJADOOA ILLAA IBLEES ABAA.\nWhen said We unto the angels “Prostrate ye in obeisance unto Adam!” they did prostrate on obeisance save ‘Iblis’; he refused.\nفَقُلْنَا يٰۤاٰدَمُ اِنَّ هٰذَا عَدُوٌّ لَّكَ وَلِزَوْجِكَ فَلَا يُخْرِجَنَّكُمَا مِنَ الْجَنَّةِ فَتَشْقٰى‏(117)\nFAQULNAA YAA AADAMO INNAL HAAZAA A’DUWWUM LAKA WALEZAWJEKA FALAA YUKHREJANNAKUMAA MENAL JANNAH FATASHQAA.\nThen said We: “O’ Adam! Verily this is an enemy unto thee and thy wife; therefore, let him not drive ye both out of the Garden for (then) thou shouldst be put to toil.\nاِنَّ لَكَ اَلَّا تَجُوْعَ فِيْهَا وَلَا تَعْرٰىۙ‏(118)\nINNAL LAKA ALLAA TAJOOA’A FEEHAA WA LAA TAA’RAA.\nFor thee it is ordained that thou shalt not be hungry in it, nor (shalt thou be) naked,\nوَاَنَّكَ لَا تَظْمَؤُا فِيْهَا وَلَا تَضْحٰى‏(119)\nWA ANNAKA LAA TAZMAUA FEEHAA WA LAA TAZHAA.\nAnd that thou shalt not be thirsty in it, nor shalt thou feel the heat of the sun.\nفَوَسْوَسَ اِلَيْهِ الشَّيْطٰنُ قَالَ يٰۤاٰدَمُ هَلْ اَدُلُّكَ عَلٰى شَجَرَةِ الْخُلْدِ وَمُلْكٍ لَّا يَبْلٰى‏(120)\nFAWASWASA ELAYHE SHAYTAANO QAALA YAA AADAMO HAL AADULLUKA A’LAA SHAJARATE AL-KHULDE WAMULKIN LAA YABLAA.\nBut Satan whispered unto him saying: “O’ Adam! shall I guide thee unto the tree of eternity and unto a kingdom which decayeth not?\nفَاَكَلَا مِنْهَا فَبَدَتْ لَهُمَا سَوْاٰ تُہُمَا وَطَفِقَا يَخْصِفٰنِ عَلَيْهِمَا مِنْ وَّرَقِ الْجَنَّةِ‌ وَعَصٰۤى اٰدَمُ رَبَّهٗ فَغَوٰى‌ۖ‏(121)\nFAAKALAA MINHAA FABADAT LAHOMAA SAWAAA TUMAA WATAFEQAA YAKHSEFAANE FEEMAF MIN WWARAQE JANNAH WAA’ASAA AADAMO WAL FAGHAWAA.\nThen they both ate of it, so their nakedness appeared unto them, and they both began to cover themselves with the leaves of the Garden; And Adam acted not (to the advices of) his Lord (deceived by Satan) and got astray.\nثُمَّ اجْتَبٰهُ رَبُّهٗ فَتَابَ عَلَيْهِ وَهَدٰى‏(122)\nSUMMA AJTABAAHU RABBOHU FA-TAABA A’LAYHE WAHADAA.\nThen his Lord chose him and turned unto him (accepting his repentance) and guided him.\nقَالَ اهْبِطَا مِنْهَا جَمِيْعًا‌ۢ بَعْضُكُمْ لِبَعْضٍ عَدُوٌّ‌ ۚ فَاِمَّا يَاْتِيَنَّكُمْ مِّنِّىْ هُدًى ۙ فَمَنِ اتَّبَعَ هُدَاىَ فَلَا يَضِلُّ وَلَا يَشْقٰى‏(123)\nQAALA AHBETAA MINHAA JAMEE-A’A BA’ZOKUM LE-BA’ZIN A’DUWWUM FA-IMMAA YAATEYANNAKUM MINNEE HODAM FAMANE’ TABA-A’L HODAAYA FALAA YAZELLU WA LAA YASHQAA.\n(And God) said: “Get down hence ye two, all together, one of you (being) the enemy unto another. So will surely come unto you guidance from Me, then whoever followed! My guidance, he shall go not astray nor put to grief\nوَمَنْ اَعْرَضَ عَنْ ذِكْرِىْ فَاِنَّ لَهٗ مَعِيْشَةً ضَنْكًا وَّنَحْشُرُهٗ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ اَعْمٰى‏(124)\nWA MAN A-A’RAZA A’N ZEKREAA FA-INNAL LAHU MAE’EESHATAN ZANKAN WWANAHSHURUH YAWMA QEYAAMATE AAA’MAA.\nAnd whoever turneth away from My monition, verily his shall be a life straitened, and We shall raise him up on the Day of Judgment, blind.\nقَالَ رَبِّ لِمَ حَشَرْتَنِىْۤ اَعْمٰى وَقَدْ كُنْتُ بَصِيْرًا‏(125)\nQAALA RABBE LEMA HASHARTANEAA AAA’MAA WA QAD KUNTO BASEERAA.\nHe shall say: “O’ my Lord! why hast thou raised me blind? Whereas indeed I was seeing (before)?\nقَالَ كَذٰلِكَ اَتَتْكَ اٰيٰتُنَا فَنَسِيْتَهَا‌ۚ وَكَذٰلِكَ الْيَوْمَ تُنْسٰى‏(126)\nQAALA KAZAALEKA AATATKA AAYAATONAA FANASEETAHAA WA KAZAALEKA YAWMA TUNSAA.\n(God) will say: “Thus (is the recompense) for did come unto thee Our signs but thou didst ignore them; And even so art thou forsaken this day\nوَكَذٰلِكَ نَجزِىْ مَنْ اَسْرَفَ وَلَمْ يُؤْمِنْۢ بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّهٖ‌ؕ وَلَعَذَابُ الْاٰخِرَةِ اَشَدُّ وَاَبْقٰى‏(127)\nWA KAZAALEKA NAJZEAA MAN AASRAFA WA LAM YO’MIM BE-AAYAATIL RABBEH LA-A’ZAABUL AAKHERATE ASHADDO WAABQAA.\nAnd thus will We recompense him who doth transgress and believeth not in the signs of his Lord; and certainly the torment of the hereafter be more severe and more lasting.\nاَفَلَمْ يَهْدِ لَهُمْ كَمْ اَهْلَكْنَا قَبْلَهُمْ مِّنَ الْقُرُوْنِ يَمْشُوْنَ فِىْ مَسٰكِنِهِمْ‌ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّاُولِى النُّهٰى‏(128)\nA-FALAM YAHDE LAHUM KAM AHLAKNAL QABLAHUM MENAL QOROONE YAMSHOONA FEE MASAAKENEHEM INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEAOOLEAA AN-NUHAA.\nWhat! Doth it guide them not aright (to know) how many of the generations We did destroy before them, amidst whose dwellings they (now) walk about? Verily, in this are signs for those (endowed) with understanding.\nوَلَوْلَا كَلِمَةٌ سَبَقَتْ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ لَكَانَ لِزَامًا وَّاَجَلٌ مُّسَمًّىؕ‏(129)\nWA LAWLAA KALEMATUN SABAQAT MIN RABBEKA LAKAANA LEZAAMAN WWAAJALUN MOSAMMAA.\nAnd had not a word (of respite) from thy Lord gone forth their arrest had immediately been ensued; And the term (of respite for them) is appointed\nفَاصْبِرْ عَلٰى مَا يَقُوْلُوْنَ وَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ قَبْلَ طُلُوْعِ الشَّمْسِ وَقَبْلَ غُرُوْبِهَا‌ ۚ وَمِنْ اٰنَآىٴِ الَّيْلِ فَسَبِّحْ وَاَطْرَافَ النَّهَارِ لَعَلَّكَ تَرْضٰى‏(130)\nFAS-BIR A’LAA MAA YAQOOLOONA WASABBEH BE-HAMDE RABBEKA QABLA TULOOE’E ASH-SHAMSE WA QABLA GHUROOBEHAA WA MIN AAANAAAA LAYLE FA-SABBEH WAATRAAFA AN-NAHAARE LAA’ALLAKA TARZAA.\nSo be thou patient with what they say, and glorify thy Lord by praising Him ere the rising of the sun and ere the setting of it; And in some hours of the night also do glorify (Him), and during parts of the day, that thou mayest achieve the pleasure (of they Lord).\nوَلَا تَمُدَّنَّ عَيْنَيْكَ اِلٰى مَا مَتَّعْنَا بِهٖۤ اَزْوَاجًا مِّنْهُمْ زَهْرَةَ الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا ۙ لِنَفْتِنَهُمْ فِيْهِ‌ ؕ وَرِزْقُ رَبِّكَ خَيْرٌ وَّاَبْقٰى‏(131)\nWA LAA TAMUDDANNA A’AYNAYKA ELAA MAA MATTAA’NAA BEHI AZWAAJANW MINHUM ZAHRATA HAYAATID DUNYAA LENAFTENAHUM FEEHE WAREZQU RABBEKA KHAYRUL KHAYRUWN.\nAnd strain not thine eyes unto that which We have provided (different) parties of them, (of) the splendour of the life of this world, so that We may try them in it; for the provision of thy Lord is better and more abiding.\nوَاْمُرْ اَهْلَكَ بِالصَّلٰوةِ وَاصْطَبِرْ عَلَيْهَا‌ ؕ لَا نَسْئَلُكَ رِزْقًا‌ ؕ نَحْنُ نَرْزُقُكَ‌ ؕ وَالْعَاقِبَةُ لِلتَّقْوٰى‏(132)\nWAAMUR AHLAKA BEALSSALAAWTE WAASTABER A’LAYHAA LAA NASALUKA RIZQAN NAHNO NARZUQUKA A-A’QEBATO LELTTAQWAA.\nAnd enjoin prayer on thy followers, and adhere thou steadily unto it, We ask thee not for subsistence; (but) We (Ourselves) give thee subsistence; and the (success of the) hereafter is for the guarding (against evil).\nوَقَالُوْا لَوْلَا يَاْتِيْنَا بِاٰيَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّهٖ ‌ؕ اَوَلَمْ تَاْتِہِمْ بَيِّنَةُ مَا فِى الصُّحُفِ الْاُوْلٰى‏(133)\nWA QAALOO LAWLAA YAATEENAA BE-AAYATIL MIN RABBEHI AWALAM TAATEM BAYNATU MAA FIL SOHOFIL OOLAA.\nAnd say they: “Why doth he not bring unto us a sign from his Lord,” What! Hath not there come unto them the clear evidence which were in the former scriptures?\nوَلَوْ اَنَّاۤ اَهْلَكْنٰهُمْ بِعَذَابٍ مِّنْ قَبْلِهٖ لَقَالُوْا رَبَّنَا لَوْلَاۤ اَرْسَلْتَ اِلَيْنَا رَسُوْلًا فَنَتَّبِعَ اٰيٰتِكَ مِنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ نَّذِلَّ وَنَخْزٰى‏(134)\nWA LAW ANNAA AHLAKNAAHUM BE-A’ZAABIN MIN QABLEHI LAQAALOOA RABBANAA LAWLAA ARSALTA ELAYNAA RASOOLAM FANATTABE-A’ AAYAATEKA MIN QABLE AN NNAZELLA WANAKHZAA.\nAnd had We destroyed them with a chastisement before him (The Apostle Muhammad) certainly would they have said: “O’ Our Lord! Why didst thou not send unto us an apostle, for then would we have followed Thy signs ere that we were (thus) humbled and disgraced.\nقُلْ كُلٌّ مُّتَرَبِّصٌ فَتَرَبَّصُوْا‌ ۚ فَسَتَعْلَمُوْنَ مَنْ اَصْحٰبُ الصِّرَاطِ السَّوِىِّ وَمَنِ اهْتَدٰى‏(135)\nQUL KULLUL MMUTARABBESUN FATARABBASOOA FA-SATA’LAMOONA MAN ASHAABUN AS-SERAATE AS-SAWEAAAE MANIT TADAA.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Every one (of us) is awaiting, so do ye (also) await: then soon ye will come to know who have been the followers of the even way and who hath been the guided aright.",
  "merits": "This Surah was revealed in Makkah and has 135 verses. It is mentioned in a narration from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that whoever recites this Surah will get the reward equivalent to the number of companions of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) from the Mohaajereen and Ansaar.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that Allah (s.w.t.) befriends the ones who recite this Surah and this person will receive his book of deeds on his right hand. His sins will be forgiven and he will get so much reward that he will be pleased on the Day of Judgement.\nThis Surah should be recited before war, going before a tyrant ruler and trying to guide a community towards the path of Allah (s.w.t.). If a girl is not getting married and she wishes to get married, she should take ghusl (bath) with water in which this Surah has been dissolved and by the will of Allah (s.w.t.) she will get married.\nIf a man wishes to get married, he should write verses 131 and 132 of this Surah with saffron and then wear it as a talisman and Inshallah his proposal will be accepted."
